**(i) Two reasons** (any two):

- Cameroon has **abundant water resources**: many large rivers (for example the Sanaga), waterfalls, a mountainous relief and heavy rainfall, which give a large and renewable hydroelectric potential ;
- once the dam is built the **running cost is low** (no fuel to buy), whereas fossil fuels are expensive, partly imported and subject to price changes ;
- hydroelectric stations **do not release carbon dioxide** or other pollutants while generating electricity, whereas burning fossil fuels pollutes the air and contributes to global warming;
- fossil fuel reserves are **limited and non-renewable**, but water is replenished by rain.

**(ii) A green source of energy:** **solar energy** (photovoltaic cells). Others: wind, geothermal energy, tidal energy, biogas (any one).
